Dear colleagues,

we refer to your draft coexistence proposal received on 6 July 2026 and to your deadline of tomorrow, 17:00 hours.

Our client Calzado Urbano Levante S.L. has considered the proposal and instructs us as follows. A limitation of class 25 to leisurewear, headgear and socks is not acceptable. Sneakers are the core product of the CAPSULA42 line, which has been presented at the Momad fair in Madrid in February 2026 and is scheduled for launch in September. Our client is, however, prepared to exclude "orthopaedic footwear" and "children's footwear" from the specification and to undertake not to use the sign in Germany and Austria for a period to be discussed, provided your client accepts full coexistence in Spain, Portugal and Italy.

Regarding class 35, our client offers to limit the online retail services to its own goods. A complete exclusion of online retail relating to shoes is not acceptable.

Our client further requires a sell-off period of twelve months for materials already produced and a mutual non-aggression undertaking covering both signs and the domain capsula42.es, which was registered on 11 March 2026.

We note that the opposition period expires on 15 September 2026. Should your client prefer to file the opposition first and continue discussions within the cooling-off period, we will not treat this as a break-off of negotiations.

We kindly ask for your comments by 31 July 2026.

